; getline_short_stack_int_register: GETLINE pops its index before it reads
; its register, so an empty stack raises StackUnderflow even though the
; register would also have been rejected.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's error-precedence rule makes operand pops first within
; every instruction. A VM that resolved the register first would raise
; TYPE_MISMATCH for programs of this shape instead of STACK_UNDERFLOW. The
; Faults table makes the identity normative, so two names for one program
; is a violation.
;
; GETLINE stands for the whole family here. The register is filled from
; calldata rather than left unset for the reason
; iter_short_stack_int_register gives: an unset register would raise
; UNSET_REGISTER and would not discriminate the order.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
GETLINE r0       ; nothing on the stack for it to pop
HALT
